schemaVersion: 1
id: stock-opportunities-reminder-root
name: Stock Opportunities Reminder
kind: root
version: 0.1.0
description: A stock scout that works for you. Each weekday it looks for stocks worth buying, says where to buy and where the idea is wrong, and keeps score of its own calls.
entry: index.md
domain: Finance

# The app this cabinet opens on. Older Cabinets open on index.md.
app: app

# Things to try in this cabinet: at most 16, each at most 80 characters.
prompts:
  - text: "Is there anything worth buying today?"
  - text: "Explain your newest call to me like I have never read a chart."
  - text: "Look at NVDA for me. Is it an opportunity or should I wait?"
  - text: "What is the market doing, and is it a good time to buy anything?"
  - text: "How did your calls do so far? Be honest."
  - text: "Why did you pass on the stocks you passed on?"
  - text: "What would have to happen for you to change your mind on your last call?"
  - text: "How do I work out how many shares to buy without risking too much?"
